creating a good user experience for  customers and the teams that maintain a  chatbot agent  are both very important and so in this  episode of deconstructing chatbots  we will share seven best practices that  will tie in key pro moves you may have  seen  in our prior lessons but we'll touch  more upon now  so stay tuned  [Music]  the first step is to future proof the  names of intents  as your agent supports a greater variety  of topics  the more successful the collaboration  with others will be  by using explicit names a common  practice is to format them as your  intention  dot expected action four common examples  of these intents  are for information collection  confirmation  supplemental questions and redirecting  to live agents  let's go through each for example when  collecting information for helping a  customer to purchase shoes for their  pups  you can name your intent choose.book to  collect parameters such as color and  size  next as a user navigates through your  flows it's good to confirm and repeat  back if the information was correct or  not  or go having two intents called  confirmation.yes  and confirmation.no are useful i will  talk more about these benefits  using confirmation yes no intents in a  bit  then there are questions that customers  may have that are not core to your  purchasing flow  but you know are frequently asked let's  call these  supplementals for example customers are  more interested in sustainability and  frequently asked pugs are your products  sustainably sourced  or may have questions about their  account and as a fourth type of intent  known as redirect.support team  is meant to allow customers to eject out  of a flow  to speak to a live person next let's  talk about reusing intents and  pages via the route group functionality  by designing your agent with reusability  in mind  it helps save time answering the same  intent from anywhere  in the journey you can do this by  creating multiple intents  and putting them together in a route  group once  and just modify every page to allow for  that same group to be used  for example you can put 100 supplemental  intents  at the beginning of a flow and at the  end  during the confirmation pages to enable  users to ask questions  outside of the flow and rebought back to  the flow after getting answers  [Music]  next you can train your agent with  phrases in bulk  by uploading them this can be done by  visiting the desired intent and  clicking the upload icon to upload a csv  or txt file  [Music]  next tip is to add rephrase variations  of questions  when you have required parameters since  it will not stop  asking this question until it gets  collected and it's good to rephrase a  question  up to three times then to pass a  customer to a human  to avoid a bad user experience if the  third try doesn't help  this is a great rule of thumb by the way  that all of us have experienced at some  point  as consumers  [Music]  and for yes no questions you want to say  did i get that  right and leverage the confirmation.yes  or no intents  this brings us to the next point it's  beneficial to reduce ambiguity by  repeating back what a person heard  as it builds trust with the user ergo by  using the money symbol  and the name of the entity in the  fulfillment section which is the reply  to the customer by the agent  you can reaffirm to the customer what  was understood from them  this applies to both the extensive list  of system entities built into dialogue  flows such as color  or date for example or custom ones you  build that you do not find as a system  entity such as size  next to enable a user to erase their  past intent for example  i want red shoes oh wait never mind  you make an intent route called go back  and make  parameter asked to null  and finally it's important to be testing  your agent as frequently as possible  when building it bit by bit  to catch errors faster you can do this  by going to the test agent functionality  on the top right side  [Music]  and there you have it seven best  practices for building a robust agent  that creates a positive user experience  both for end users and those who  maintain the agent  i hope to see you in the next episode  for deconstructing chat bots  if you like this video and would like to  see more of such content  don't forget to like and subscribe as  well as to check out the  helpful links i have listed in this  video's description cheers and thank you  for watching  you
 

